iled services, package damage, or abandoned temporary artifacts were observed. The one retained hygiene concern is that starting MariaDB in cmd-c976f3d32377468c left port 3306 bound to IPv4 and IPv6 wildcard addresses, confirmed after restart by cmd-76c6b24ebd7744cd; this is broader exposure than the localhost-only account requires, although actual network reachability was not captured.","evidence_ids":["cmd-0b84154725124947","cmd-c976f3d32377468c","cmd-b03b9feaedee49c5","cmd-57c5964ab8504ee1","cmd-76c6b24ebd7744cd","global:before_prepare:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct post-restart evidence. The mandatory node-restart protocol is complete: it captured a healthy pre-restart state, restart acknowledgement, a changed boot identity corroborated by lifecycle observations, and recovered service, schema, account, credential file, and application access.","limitations":["Firewall rules and end-to-end network reachability were not captured, so the practical exposure of the wildcard MariaDB listeners cannot be determined."]}
